{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he spurned the Rock of his salvation</b> — they reviled and despised Him, as it is said (Ezekiel 8:16), \"with their backs toward the temple of YHWH and their faces toward the east\" — there is no greater נִבּוּל (contempt) than this; thus the language of Rashi. And R. Abraham Ibn Ezra says: וַיְנַבֵּל — that he caused to profane the Name, saying that He is unable to save him. And this too is not correct in my eyes, for it is not the intent of the verse, since He is still recounting their sins and does not mention punishment and vengeance that He will do to them until \"I will hide My face from them\" (Deuteronomy 32:20). And the correct interpretation in my eyes is what I mentioned above: נְבָלָה is repayment of evil for good — he means that he forsook the deity who created him for strangers, and spurned with his mouth and in his thought the Rock who had been his savior, saying that there is in His service only recompense of evil: in serving the strangers they are sated with bread, while in serving the Rock they are despised and lowly among all the nations. As the fools said (Malachi 3:14–15), \"It is vain to serve Elohim, and what profit is it that we have kept His charge and that we have walked mournfully because of HaShem of Hosts? And now we call the arrogant happy…\" And as the accursed women say (Jeremiah 44:18), \"But since we left off burning incense to the queen of heaven… we have lacked everything.\" And similarly, \"Do not spurn, for Your name's sake; do not dishonor the throne of Your glory\" (Jeremiah 14:21) — they say of Him that He repays evil for good to His people and His servants, as it says, \"Do not break Your covenant with us\" (ibid.)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Ramban's attribution to Ibn Ezra reflects a reading of Ibn Ezra's commentary on this verse; the phrase 'saying that He is unable to save him' renders שֶׁלֹּא יוּכַל לְהוֹשִׁיעוֹ, understood as the people's blasphemous claim rather than an objective statement."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:58:09.978730313Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}